libhimmelblau is an interoperability library for Microsoft Entra ID (formerly
Azure Active Directory) and Microsoft Intune.  It implements the protocols a
device needs to register with Entra ID, to obtain and refresh tokens, and to
enrol with and report to Intune.

The library is written in Rust but is built with cargo-c, so it installs a
shared library, a C header generated by cbindgen, and a pkg-config file.  It
can therefore be used from C and from other languages, not only from Rust.

It is developed by the Samba team and is the protocol layer underneath
Himmelblau, which provides Entra ID authentication for Unix systems.
